375 0 obj
<<
/Title (Limitations: \(i\) the included observations are synthetic, \(ii\) study hours are self-reported, \(iii\) the dashboard is descriptive rather than predictive, \(iv\) the statistical thresholds are exploratory, and \(v\) valid student identifiers are anonymised but the application has no user accounts or access controls. Additionally, grades use a fixed threshold scheme that may not match every institution.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 334 0 R
/Next 417 0 R
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project demonstrates a complete workflow for inspecting student study hours and assessment scores: CSV handling, record validation, object-oriented design, NumPy statistics, Pandas course aggregation, Matplotlib charts and a Tkinter dashboard. On the included synthetic data, a positive association persists after excluding IQR-flagged outliers, but the strength of the Pearson correlation changes substantially. The central analytical conclusion is therefore cautious: the dashboard can reveal and communicate patterns, but it cannot determine that study hours cause assessment results.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 334 0 R
/Prev 418 0 R
>>
endobj
